      "name": "Tar Splatter",
      "img": "icons/magic/symbols/runes-carved-stone-green.webp",
      "effects": [],
      "sort": 200,
      "ownership": {
        "default": 0
      },
      "flags": {},
      "type": "feat",
      "system": {
        "description": {
          "value": "<p>The first time each turn when the targoyle takes Bludgeoning, Piercing, or Slashing damage, it bursts in an eruption of scalding tar. <em>Saving Throw:</em> DC 16 Dexterity, each creature in a 15-foot Emanation originating from the targoyle. <em>Failure:</em> The target is coated in tar until it or a creature within reach of it takes an action to remove the tar. While coated in tar, a creature's Speed is reduced by 15 feet. If a creature coated in tar takes Fire damage, it takes an extra 9 (2d8) Fire damage and is no longer coated in tar.</p>",
          "chat": ""
        },
